    "q-37755": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37755",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}-13x-5 \\\\  & -x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-6{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,13{x}^{2}-21x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{13{x}^{2}-26x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10}{-x+2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}-13x-5 \\\\  & -x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-6{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,13{x}^{2}-21x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{13{x}^{2}-26x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10$ by the linear binomial $-x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient $6{x}^{2}-13x-5,$ and\n\n- the remainder $20.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10}{-x+2}=6{x}^{2}-13x-5+\\frac{20}{-x+2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
