    "q-38072": {
      "dom_id": "step-q38072",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4x+3 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x+6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11}{x+2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4x+3 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x+6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial ${x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11$ by the linear binomial $x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${x}^{2}+4x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $5.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11}{x+2}={x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{5}{x+2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
