    "q-37964": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37964",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x-9} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+0x-9\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-2 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x-9} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,2x-4}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2x-4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
